    "narrative": "For this May 28th slate, **Daulton Varsho** and **Taylor Ward** headline our active roster as the only two hitters currently cleared for action, both comfortably entrenched in the \"Strong\" category. **Daulton Varsho** secures the daily ceiling at 72.31, bolstered by a favorable matchup against Bassitt. The combination of a high-value #4 order spot and a positive park adjustment pushes **Daulton Varsho** into must-start territory, as his dynamic platoon splits against right-handed pitching remain a critical component of our offensive engine. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** earns a 71.46 efficiency score. While he faces the lefty Corbin, his role as the table-setter out of the #1 hole and a favorable park environment offset the handedness risk, ensuring **Taylor Ward** provides the necessary volume to chase those elusive R and RBI totals.\n\nThe roster remains thinned by a series of off-days and injuries, necessitating caution with our daily game caps. Our bench is currently headlined by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Lawrence Butler**, all of whom are unavailable due to team off-days. Furthermore, **Cal Raleigh** remains a critical absence while on the IL, leaving us without his power upside. We are monitoring the status of the rest of our depth\u2014including **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Bryson Stott**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014for future availability. With limited volume tonight, the priority remains protecting our seasonal caps while leaning on the favorable projections of **Daulton Varsho** and **Taylor Ward** to maintain our momentum in the 5x5 standings.",
